From 393f6be028fb0a5a9b9c1eb7ebf73bcdc5da3ff3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 00:25:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix Sold out not applying + make the item search a live
 lookup

Sold-out flags were stored against one id space but applied against another:
preset-built menu items use a 'preset:<id>' menu id while the admin's Sold-out
list keyed overrides by the raw Square item id, so a flag never matched the
menu item and nothing went sold out on the storefront.

- Server applyAvailability now matches a manual override / day-exclusion by the
  menu item's id OR its underlying Square source id (presetSourceItemId), so a
  flag lands whichever id it was saved under.
- Admin Sold-out list and the day-exclusion add-picker now use the app's OFFERED
  menu items (menu ids incl. preset ids) instead of the raw Square product list,
  so a new flag is stored under the id the customer menu is built from and takes
  effect immediately. The list also shows the real menu items, so the
  search-as-you-type box actually finds them.
- /api/admin/offered-products returns each item's sourceId; the admin reflects
  and can clear a legacy raw-id flag, and toggling clears the source-id override
  too so a stale flag can't keep an item stuck sold out.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
